# Generated by `make webdata` from the Phase 1 ETL output (docs/adr/002) —
# regenerate, never hand-edit or commit large data exports.
#
# TEMPORARY EXCEPTION (2026-09-07, docs/STATE.md "Data source for tonight's
# deploy"): data/etl/ isn't committed, so a fresh Cloudflare Pages checkout
# has no ETL output to export from. Building all 12 cities' real data in
# Cloudflare's own build step (network fetch from Overture + DuckDB
# scoring) was explicitly ruled out for this deploy as its own
# architecture decision, not a "quick fix" -- see the runbook. Owner
# decision: commit a frozen snapshot instead, un-ignored below, so
# Cloudflare's build is just `npm run build`. This makes the exception
# explicit rather than silently un-ignoring files with no trace of why.
# Re-freshing this snapshot (or replacing it with a real pipeline) is a
# separate decision -- do not silently regenerate and recommit without
# that decision being made again.
#
# UPDATED 2026-09-08 (docs/adr/013, night mission #2 Bloc A): the frozen
# snapshot grows from the 2-city hardcoded set to all 12 launch cities'
# static-subset hotel sets, per that ADR -- this IS the decision above
# being revisited, explicitly, not a silent regeneration. Cloudflare's
# build command is unchanged (`npm run build`, no Python, no network).
!src/data/hotels-*.json
!src/data/city-baselines.json
!src/data/personas.json
!src/data/meta.json
!src/data/city-pages.json
!public/data/search-index.json
!public/data/search-index-*.json

